 "note": "Lunenburg High School staff, identified by the 'SCHOOL STAFF' heading on line 19 and the 'High School Principal' heading under it. Lines 1-18 are the end of the high school narrative (NEASC); line 52 is the page number. Three columns (Textract x 0.12 / 0.40 / 0.64), each a run of section headings with names beneath; names were assigned to columns by x position, not by order in the row. Headings that name a single post (High School Principal, Assistant Principal, Administrative Secretary, Attendance Clerk, Computer Coordinator, Nurse, Director of Athletics) go in role_raw; department headings (Mathematics, English, Science, Guidance, Special Education ...) go in grade_or_dept. Text printed with a person -- '(Chair)', '(Coordinator)', ', Gr. 9&11', ', Secretary', ', Director' -- is kept in role_raw. Lines 20, 26 and 50 hold only headings; other heading cells share a row with names and those rows are claimed by their entries."
